<p>A suspected Iranian drone strike hit the grounds next to the U.S. consulate in Dubai on March 3, sparking a fire and sending black smoke into the air, according to U.S. officials and Dubai’s government media office. Officials said there were no reported injuries, and all U.S. personnel were safe and accounted for. Dubai authorities said they contained the blaze and later extinguished it. The incident comes as Iran launches missile and drone attacks across the Gulf in retaliation for a major U.S.-Israeli military campaign inside Iran, with multiple American diplomatic sites reportedly targeted in recent days.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oRO-DVCxWuSTySQZbaHcevHF9oxmqT4o3-cJOSYU1UyUNYAo3J-DaQn2BFC2M3qaUkuE63DGB7lAlbSQIOz1oCCgTemZ4_9Yo-FDzTykPnqmZ-iyQQ0AiY3b-K5lle29bgh6nWhgqBjuIyQ8NtjHQIOqa_KEcyoInO_BkcRapPKMYSNXpE8lQl4KWA' alt='Smoke rises near the U.S. consulate area in Dubai after a reported drone-related incident.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Riyadh attacks: People familiar with the matter said the U.S. Embassy in Riyadh was attacked twice on Tuesday, including a strike that caused part of a roof to collapse.</li><li>UAE hit hardest: CBS News said the United Arab Emirates has been targeted more than any other Gulf nation during Tehran’s recent campaign.</li><li>Witness accounts and video: Euronews said residents heard a loud explosion as smoke and flames rose, and police set up a security perimeter near the consulate.</li><li>Conflict trigger: Time said Iran’s barrage follows a massive U.S.-Israeli campaign that killed Iran’s Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei.</li></ul><blockquote>Our embassies and our diplomatic facilities are under direct attack from a terroristic regime, - Marco Rubio</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. State Department (Marco Rubio): Rubio said the U.S. had cut staffing to “bare bones” as threats spread, and said U.S. diplomatic facilities were being targeted across the region. (<a href='https://time.com/7382378/iran-war-us-consulate-drone-strike-retaliatory-attacks/'>Time</a>)</li><li>Dubai Government Media Office: Dubai’s media office said the fire from a “drone-related incident” near the consulate was contained and later extinguished, and that no injuries were reported. (<a href='https://time.com/7382378/iran-war-us-consulate-drone-strike-retaliatory-attacks/'>Time</a>)</li><li>PBS NewsHour: PBS framed the strike in Dubai as part of widening Iranian attacks across Gulf states as U.S. and Israeli jets continue attacks inside Iran. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/as-u-s-escalates-attacks-iran-hits-american-diplomatic-targets-in-middle-east'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>AllSides summary: AllSides highlighted reports that U.S. diplomatic missions are coming under fire, including claims that the U.S. Embassy in Riyadh was hit twice and that part of a roof collapsed. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-03-0800/middle-east-drone-targets-us-consulate-dubai-iran-escalates-attacks'>AllSides</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/fire-near-us-consulate-in-dubai-after-drone-attack-govt-statement/article70701012.ece'>Fire near U.S. consulate in Dubai after drone attack: govt statement</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-03-0800/middle-east-drone-targets-us-consulate-dubai-iran-escalates-attacks'>Drone Targets U.S. Consulate in Dubai as Iran Escalates Attacks</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/us-consulate-grounds-in-dubai-set-ablaze-by-suspected-iranian-drone-strike/'>U.S. consulate grounds in Dubai set ablaze by suspected Iranian drone strike</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7382378/iran-war-us-consulate-drone-strike-retaliatory-attacks/'>Suspected Iranian Drone Strikes Near U.S. Consulate in Dubai</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/as-u-s-escalates-attacks-iran-hits-american-diplomatic-targets-in-m